From c583fbfc765eb043d0fb1f070b1642261c7aa81d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 07:27:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license_files to cover the vendored libssh licence

setup.cfg's explicit license_files list only names LICENSE.rst, so
setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E* glob never applies here and a dropped-in
LICENSE.<dep> is silently ignored. The Linux/macOS wheels link libssh
dynamically and auditwheel/delocate vendor its shared library into the
wheel (confirmed on the official ansible_pylibssh-1.4.0 manylinux_x86_64
wheel on PyPI, which ships libssh's compiled .so but none of its LGPL-2.1
licence text), so every architecture's wheel is missing it, not just
riscv64's.

Widening the list to LICENSE.* lets LICENSE.libssh and LICENSE.libssh-bsd,
staged at the project root during the build, reach dist-info/licenses/
with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every ansible-pylibssh wheel on PyPI regardless of architecture, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 52304c0..ae69d66 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ author_email = info+github/ansible/pylibssh@ansible.com
 license = LGPLv2+
 license_files =
   LICENSE.rst
+  LICENSE.*
 classifiers =
   Development Status :: 2 - Pre-Alpha
 
-- 
